ES moduleClassic global <pre><code>import { VexyVlip } from "vexy-vlip-js";

const stage = document.querySelector("#stage");
const vlip = new VexyVlip(stage, {
  src: "demo.mp4",
  track: "demo.vtt",
  mode: "stepped",   // "continuous" | "stepped"
  controls: true,
});

// Methods can be called at once; the track loads asynchronously.
document.querySelector("#next").addEventListener("click", () =&gt; vlip.next());

// Events bubble from the container element.
stage.addEventListener("vexyvlip:stop", (e) =&gt; {
  console.log("paused at segment", e.detail.index);
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;script src="vexy-vlip.global.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
  // window.VexyVlip is the class; &lt;vexy-vlip&gt; is also registered.
  const vlip = new VexyVlip(document.querySelector("#stage"), {
    src: "demo.mp4",
    track: "demo.vtt",
    mode: "continuous",
  });
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre> <p>The container you pass to the constructor receives the class <code>vexy-vlip</code>, a <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> element, and the card layer. If you pass an existing <code>&lt;video&gt;</code> element instead, the player wraps it in a new <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> and uses that as the container.</p>
